<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill avg yield rises to 13.18 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill avg yield rises to 13.18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills rose to 13.18 percent at an auction on June 24 from 10.97 percent at the previous auction on June 17, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   June 24	    June 17</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K2509976     KZ43K1809971</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  500		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 991		  1,320</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 500		  536</p>
<p> Average price			 96.81 pct	  97.33</p>
<p> Average yield			 13.18		10.97</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Sep 25, 1997     Sep 18, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410 $=75.465 tenge</p>
